121:- `contract-performance` — direct: Sprint 34 declares performance expectations, bounds expensive work, and avoids speculative concurrency. The shared-prompt renderer declares a 256 KiB prefix budget and 64 KiB suffix reserve (`internal/sprint/prompt_context.go:18-21`); tests prove exact boundary behavior at 256 KiB fit, one-byte overflow, and 64 KiB suffix reserve (`internal/sprint/prompt_context_test.go:186-262`). Source resolution is sequential, symlink-rejecting, regular-file-only, bounded by per-reference and aggregate byte budgets, and cancellation-aware via `ctx.Err()` checks before each reference, inside `readSharedLineRange`, and before return (`internal/sprint/prompt_context.go:127-196, 312-392`); no recursive scan, no goroutines, no unbounded `os.ReadFile`. Review fan-out uses `workers = min(Concurrency, len(runCoverage))` with a 1-16 cap (default 3), bounded channels, `sync.WaitGroup`, and `TestReviewFanOutUsesConfiguredBound` (`internal/sprint/review.go:174-187, 487-533, 589-603`). Execute reuses one `sharedPrefix` across tasks with `sync.Mutex` for `task.Runtime` (`internal/sprint/execute.go:217-231`). Smoke authoring caps snapshots at `maxSmokeAuthoringFiles = 20000` files and 64 MiB per file via `filepath.WalkDir` (`internal/sprint/smoke_author.go:18, 197-203, 302-343`). No caching, retrieval, index, or persistence is introduced; the architecture explicitly documents that no provider cache hit is guaranteed or measured (`docs/architecture.md:147`). Cost drivers (model, model_source, project, sprint, stage, task, coverage, run, session) are attached to every runtime request (`internal/sprint/service.go:983-1033`). `PERF-UI-001` is not triggered: this sprint does not change UI/TUI rendering; the web facade bounds are documented elsewhere and unchanged. All performance-sensitive constraints are declared, bounded, tested, and aligned with the Performance Contract; no actionable deviation found.
124:- `contract-testing` — direct: The Sprint 34 implementation conforms to the testing contract. The new shared-prefix renderer (`target/internal/sprint/prompt_context.go:126-197`) has dedicated unit tests in `target/internal/sprint/prompt_context_test.go` covering exact-byte preservation, LF/CRLF/no-final-newline artifacts, deterministic authored-order with duplicates and overlaps (`prompt_context_test.go:55-76`), fail-closed source resolution across escape/absolute/missing/symlink/directory/out-of-range classes (`prompt_context_test.go:78-112`), cancellation, encoding, and budget errors (`prompt_context_test.go:129-151`), mid-read replacement detection (`prompt_context_test.go:153-184`), exact 256 KiB fit and one-byte overflow (`prompt_context_test.go:186-210`), recursion and mutation absence (`prompt_context_test.go:212-243`), and legacy suffix compatibility plus budget enforcement (`prompt_context_test.go:245-262`). Cross-stage integration is proved by `prompt_context_test.go:264-308` and `prompt_context_test.go:310-372`, which capture previews and runtime requests for sprint-index, technical-handbook, area-reasoning, final reasoning, plan, and execute and assert byte-for-byte identical prefixes with one stage boundary and no dynamic values. Cumulative flow coverage at `target/internal/sprint/sprint_index_test.go:175-196` locks in the canonical ordering with code-context scheduled exactly once. Review fan-out, citation, validation, repair, permission, restart, resume, fingerprint, atomic write, cancellation, blocked preflight, and drift diagnostics are covered by `target/internal/sprint/review_test.go:127-649`. Smoke authoring shared-prefix placement and stage-specific manifest exclusion are covered by `target/internal/sprint/smoke_test.go:282-414`. Skill materialization, customization preservation, force restoration, single-stage isolation, manual-only metadata, and canonical CLI delegation are covered by `target/internal/workspace/skills_test.go:10-230`. TEST-SEAM-001 holds: every collaborator is replaced through public `WithRuntime`, `WithStageRuntime`, `WithReviewConcurrency`, `WithProcessRunner`, `WithSmokeSettings`, and `WithRuntimeProgress` seams; no test mutates private service fields. TEST-FAIL-001 holds: every failure path introduced by the renderer (invalid path, containment, file kind, missing source, invalid range, changed read, encoding, budget, cancellation) is mapped to an explicit test. TEST-DET-001 holds: tests use `t.TempDir()`, deterministic fake runtimes, byte-equality assertions on stable slices, and lifecycle/state assertions. TEST-INT-001 holds: composition changes are exercised through integration tests that build full runtime requests via fake runtimes. TEST-CONTRACT-001 holds: `review_test.go:326-342` keeps a subprocess prompt-budget compatibility check, `review_test.go:344-381` validates verdict and citation gates, and `review_test.go:383-408` covers legacy deferred normalization plus duplicate-id rejection. TEST-E2E-001 holds for sprint flow ordering and shared-prefix reuse, and the gated real-repository requirements-to-plan dogfood required by `plan.md:159` is recorded as a truthful blocker in `execute.md:89-95` because the active manual execute skill permits only project status, sprint status, and execute-prompt CLI use; the blocked status names the exact missing prerequisite and is not represented as a pass. The release verification transcript in `execute.md:71-79` records `go test ./internal/sprint`, `go test ./internal/workspace ./internal/app ./internal/tui ./internal/web`, `go test ./...`, `go test -race ./...`, `go vet ./...`, `go build ./cmd/ultraplan`, and `git diff --check` as passing, satisfying the race and static-analysis expectations in `plan.md:152-158`. No actionable deviations from the testing contract were identified.
